# text = The question before the Committee is , whether a young man of very fair family , good appearance , and some talent , makes a fool or a wise man of himself in marrying a female waterman , turned factory girl Hardly so , I think I take the question to be , whether such a man as you describe , Lady Tippins , does right or wrong in marrying a brave woman ( I say nothing of her beauty ), who has saved his life , with a wonderful energy and address ; whom he knows to be virtuous , and possessed of remarkable qualities ; whom he has long admired , and who is deeply attached to him But , excuse me was this young woman ever a female waterman Never .
